 "notes": "Rows 66r l.10-13 (image 0084_0136) and 66v l.1 (image 0084_0137): 14 + 18 + 14 + 16 + 10 = 72, as the record; لسانه runs over the page turn (ل س | ا ن ه). Plain 1.3-1.4x half-line zooms, 2.2-2.5x on look-alikes. Every sign takes one letter: the sin-cup is alif (14), the 3-shape ه (6), the 8-loop ن (6), the circle م (4), Π ت (4). The doubtful word: 5 signs, Π ൻ + ᘐ Π, which the key reads ت ذ ب ل ت: the root is ذبل (languish, of the eyes: اذا ذبلت عيناه), with ت where the record has ان (the clear text is unclear between اندبلت and انذبلت). Keyed as تذبلت; the key has no ambiguity there (Π is ت in تهواه and امتص, the triple arch ذ in اذا, the cross ب in اطيب and وقبل, ᘐ ل in والنعاس, لسانه, وقبل). The loop-on-a-stem signs are three shapes by their side stroke: plain curve ق (قد, وقبل), teeth to the right غ, teeth to the left ش. The bar of the ب has the upright above it only in اطيب and through it in تذبلت and وقبل: one shape."
